& [Delineation]
  + compact UTF-8 JSON bytes are a deterministic serialization measure and not tokens context utilization latency memory or reasoning quality
  + model-facing exchange includes public requests and sanitized fixture responses but excludes exact registry and record custody
  + projection payload means the unique READY and terminal projections rather than every repeated serialized occurrence in later transcript requests
  + exact terminal custody means terminal observation plus final registry serialization and intentionally reports its component sizes separately
  + complete wrapper size is retained artifact size and not runtime resident memory

& [SelectedForms]
  + one PassByteMeasurement per exact phase with zero-based index request response and cumulative-request bytes
  + one IterativeTranscriptMeasurement with checked totals component sizes three ratios explicit basis and nonclaims
  + derive all values from one deterministic pending fixture and its valid admitted reflection completion
  + strict validator checks ordering arithmetic expected pass count ratios size relationships and compiled boundary strings
  + CLI emits only pretty normalized measurement JSON to stdout

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty names bytes without upgrading them to tokens speed accuracy or quality
  + Security keeps exact registry and record outside model-facing classification
  + Planner checks ordered phase count cumulative sums and total arithmetic
  + Weaver relates transcript growth projection transport pending custody and complete artifact
  + Scribe records reproducible numeric evidence and byte basis
  + Refiner exposes ratios only when numerator denominator and interpretation are exact
  + Observer admits the artifact only when generator validator CLI and checked-in bytes agree

